    "py": "def loop_start(fuel, cost):\n    total = tank = start = 0\n    for i, (gain, burn) in enumerate(zip(fuel, cost)):\n        total += gain - burn\n        tank += gain - burn\n        if tank < 0:\n            start = i + 1\n            tank = 0\n    return -1 if total < 0 else start\n",
    "explanation": "If the van starting at s runs dry leaving depot j, every start k between s and j fails too: the s run reached k with a non-negative tank, so starting at k with an empty tank leaves no more fuel at any later depot. So the candidate jumps to j + 1. If the total gain is non-negative, the last candidate also covers the wrapped-around prefix, since that prefix's deficit is at most the surplus it built up."
